`DArcane D`cue`Cl`cin`Dg Circle`x~
Circular markings define the `wdueling ground`x, their lines interrupted by
old scuffs. Near the middle, repeated contests have worn a duller patch into
the surface. The circle edge leaves observers room to gather, with the marked
boundary making every step into the open ground feel deliberate. A broad panel
presents a simple diagram of the activity, with the surrounding finish kept
spare. The floor changes texture just beyond the main playing surface, making
the limit apparent underfoot.`x
